<title>ITALY: Ambroveneto cuts prime to 10 percent.</title>
<headline>Ambroveneto cuts prime to 10 percent.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Banco Ambrosiano Veneto said on Thursday it cut its prime rate to 10 percent from 10.75 percent with effect from Friday.</p>
<p>An official at the bank said it would also cut its top lending rate to 17.75 percent from 18.50 percent.</p>
<p>The move follows the Bank of Italy's reduction in its discount rate on Wednesday from 8.25 percent to 7.50 percent. Milan newsroom +392-66102321</p>
